## Key Concepts

- RBAC and DLP enforcement across tenants
- Tamper-evident audit logs (sequencing, signatures/HMAC)
- End-to-end data export redaction
- Seeds and mocks for deterministic, isolated tests
- Flaky service handling and time-based retention checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo end-to-end test sketch (Playwright/Cypress-agnostic)
async function testRBACAndDLP() {
  const t = seedTenant('tenantA');
  const uOwner = seedUser(t, 'owner');
  const uEditor = seedUser(t, 'editor');
  const uAuditor = seedUser(t, 'auditor');
  const admin = seedUser(t, 'admin');

  // Owner creates a share with PII
  await login(uOwner);
  await createShare({ tenant: t.id, data: 'PII' });

  // Editor attempts restricted action
  await login(uEditor);
  assertAccessDenied(editShare(t.id));

  // Auditor reads audit trail
  await login(uAuditor);
  assertAuditIncludes(t.id, 'READ', uAuditor.id);

  // Admin exports with redaction
  await login(admin);
  const exportPayload = await exportData(t.id);
  assertRedacts(exportPayload, ['PII']);
  // Verify tamper-evident log
  assertTamperEvidence(t.id);
}
```
